  - bookmaker margin
  - odds
  - forecasting
  - calibration
  - open data
abstract: >-
  Daily snapshots, since 20 June 2026, of the public track record of football (soccer) 1X2
  predictions published by TipsAudit, each logged before kick-off, with the sharp-market
  (Pinnacle) price recorded for the prediction, the devigged fair probability of the pick, the
  closing price, the prediction's closing-line value (raw Pinnacle price against the raw
  Pinnacle close, not devigged), the settled result and the value flag if there is one. Also
  includes a monthly CSV of the settled predictions that adds the devigged fair probabilities of
  all three outcomes, the best price at other bookmakers (two betting exchanges included) and
  the bookmaker margin on each match (columns and caveats in datasets/README.md), daily
  bookmaker-margin measurements (betting exchanges included) and the frozen specifications of
  pre-registered forward experiments. Timestamped snapshots are never overwritten; each is
  listed with its SHA-256 in manifest.csv and submitted to OpenTimestamps when published. A
  weekly upgrade adds the Bitcoin attestation to those proofs, so the newest proofs may still be
  pending. The Git history shows any difference between snapshots; CORRECTIONS.md describes the
  corrections we announced. Value flags before 26 September 2026 are a reconstruction (a
  backtest), not a record of what the site showed at the time (see CORRECTIONS.md).
date-released: "2026-06-20"
